IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Code of the District of Columbia, Title 47, Chapter 18 -- the individual income tax of a RESIDENT for a calendar taxable
-- year from 2022: "resident" (s 47-1801.04(42)); who must file (s 47-1805.02(1)); taxable income (s 47-1806.01) with the
-- standard deduction (s 47-1801.04(44)) and the personal exemptions and their phase-out (s 47-1806.02(h), (h-1), (i)); the
-- rates (s 47-1806.03(a)(11), (c), (e)); the DC earned income tax credit (s 47-1806.04(f)); the child tax credit
-- (s 47-1806.17); the date to file and pay (s 47-1805.03(a)(2), s 47-1812.07(a)(1)); extensions (s 47-1805.03(b)); payment
-- of a deficiency (s 47-1812.07(a)(3)); and the appeal of a deficiency to the Superior Court (s 47-1815.01).
--
-- SEAT: the individual taxpayer resident in the District. "Am I a DC resident? Must I file? How much is my tax, my earned
-- income credit and my child tax credit? Do I get the EITC in monthly payments? By when must I file and pay? I have been
-- assessed a deficiency: by when must I pay or appeal?" The Chief Financial Officer and the Mayor appear only as what they
-- may or must do to the taxpayer.
--
-- Edition: Code of the District of Columbia, "through 2026-09-26" (last codified D.C. Law 26-187), from the Council's bulk
-- XML (github.com/DCCouncil/law-xml-codified, branch publication/2026-05-23, commit 9c950ac5), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/dc-code-47-ch18-subch-i-vi-individual-income-tax-2026-10.txt and
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/dc-code-47-ch18-subch-xii-xvi-assessment-collection-2026-10.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19).
-- The text is deposited for public reference and for encoding the law as rules, not for model training (the Council's
-- robots.txt signals ai-train=no).
--
-- Read with the Internal Revenue Code baseline (../../../../internal-revenue-code-of-1986/encodings/baseline-2026-10/): the
-- standard deduction "prescribed in section 63(c)" (s 47-1801.04(44)(iv)), the personal exemption amount "prescribed in section
-- 151" (s 47-1806.02(i)(2)), whether a federal return is required (IRC s 6012), the federal earned income credit and, for a
-- worker with no qualifying child, its credit percentage and earned income amount (IRC s 32), and "qualifying child" (IRC
-- ss 24(c), 32) are INPUTS here. DC adjusted gross income (s 47-1803.02) is an INPUT too: its inclusions and exclusions are
-- not encoded.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: nonresidents and part-year residents (fractional-year proration in ss 47-1801.04(44)(D), 47-1806.02(g),
-- 47-1806.04(f)(2), 47-1806.17(b)(3)); years before 2022; the counting of exemptions (s 47-1806.02(b) to (f): the number is
-- an input); itemized deductions (the amount is an input); the low income credit (s 47-1806.04(e)) and every other credit,
-- including Schedule H (s 47-1806.06); the noncustodial parent EITC (s 47-1806.04(g)); the cost-of-living adjustments of the
-- childless EITC phase-out amount and of the child tax credit after 2025 (not deposited: inputs or `not covered`);
-- withholding and estimated tax; penalties and interest (subchapter XIII is repealed; the rules now sit elsewhere in Title 47,
-- not deposited).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the taxpayer's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `District of Columbia individual income tax -- a resident`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `only taxable years beginning after December 31, 2021 are encoded (s 47-1806.03(a)(11))`
    `the tax on a nonresident or part-year resident is not encoded`
    `the child tax credit after 2025 is increased by a cost-of-living adjustment that is not deposited (s 47-1806.17(b)(1)(B))`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `s 47-1801.04(42) -- resident`

-- s 47-1801.04(42): "'Resident' means an individual domiciled in the District at any time during the taxable year, and every
-- other individual who maintains a place of abode within the District for an aggregate of 183 days or more during the taxable
-- year, whether or not the individual is domiciled in the District, excluding any elective officer of the government of the
-- United States or any employee on the staff of an elected official in the legislative branch ... if the employee is a bona
-- fide resident of the state of residence of the elected officer, or any officer of the executive branch ... whose appointment
-- was made by the President ... subject to confirmation by the Senate ... or any Justice of the Supreme Court ..., unless the
-- officer, employee, or justice is domiciled within the District at any time during the taxable year."
GIVEN `domiciled in the District at any time during the taxable year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days maintaining a place of abode in the District` IS A NUMBER
      `an excluded federal officer, congressional staff member resident in the member's state, presidential appointee or Justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a resident of the District` IF
        `domiciled in the District at any time during the taxable year`
    OR  (    `days maintaining a place of abode in the District` AT LEAST 183
         AND (NOT `an excluded federal officer, congressional staff member resident in the member's state, presidential appointee or Justice`))

§§ `s 47-1806.02 -- personal exemptions`

-- (i)(2): "For taxable years beginning after December 31, 2017, the personal exemption amount prescribed in section 151 of the
-- Internal Revenue Code of 1986 without reduction for the phaseout of section 151(d)(3)". An input.
-- (h): for an individual for whom a deduction "is allowable to another taxpayer", "the exemption amount ... shall be zero".
-- (h-1): "(1) ... the amount of the personal exemption otherwise allowable ... in the case of an individual whose adjusted gross
-- income exceeds $150,000 shall be reduced by 2% for every $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross
-- income for the taxable year exceeds $150,000. (2) No amount of the personal exemption ... shall be available for an adjusted
-- gross income in excess of $275,000." (At $275,000 the reduction is 50 steps of 2%: 100%.)
GIVEN `the number of exemptions` IS A NUMBER
      `the federal personal exemption amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
      `the taxpayer is another's dependent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the DC personal exemptions for` `the number of exemptions` `of` `the federal personal exemption amount` `at adjusted gross income` `the adjusted gross income` `when another's dependent` `the taxpayer is another's dependent` MEANS
    IF   `the taxpayer is another's dependent` OR `the adjusted gross income` GREATER THAN 275000
    THEN 0
    ELSE max 0 (`the full amount` MINUS (`the full amount` TIMES min 1 (2% TIMES `the steps`)))
    WHERE
        `the full amount` MEANS `the number of exemptions` TIMES `the federal personal exemption amount`
        `the steps` MEANS
            IF   `the adjusted gross income` GREATER THAN 150000
            THEN CEILING ((`the adjusted gross income` MINUS 150000) DIVIDED BY 2500)
            ELSE 0

§§ `s 47-1806.03(a)(11) -- the rates`

-- "In the case of taxable years beginning after December 31, 2021, there is imposed on the taxable income of every resident a
-- tax determined in accordance with the following table: Not over $10,000: 4% of the taxable income; Over $10,000 but not over
-- $40,000: $400, plus 6% of the excess over $10,000; Over $40,000 but not over $60,000: $2,200, plus 6.5% of the excess over
-- $40,000; Over $60,000 but not over $250,000: $3,500, plus 8.5% of the excess over $60,000; Over $250,000 but not over
-- $500,000: $19,650, plus 9.25% of the excess over $250,000; Over $500,000 but not over $1,000,000: $42,775, plus 9.75% of the
-- excess over $500,000; Over $1,000,000: $91,525, plus 10.75% of the excess over $1,000,000". One table for every filing
-- status: (c) a person not living with a spouse on the last day is single; (e) spouses filing separately are each single.
DECLARE `DC table row` HAS
    `over`        IS A NUMBER
    `base amount` IS A NUMBER
    `rate`        IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A LIST OF `DC table row`
`the (a)(11) table` MEANS
    LIST (`DC table row` OF 0,       0,     4%)
       , (`DC table row` OF 10000,   400,   6%)
       , (`DC table row` OF 40000,   2200,  6.5%)
       , (`DC table row` OF 60000,   3500,  8.5%)
       , (`DC table row` OF 250000,  19650, 9.25%)
       , (`DC table row` OF 500000,  42775, 9.75%)
       , (`DC table row` OF 1000000, 91525, 10.75%)

GIVEN `the taxable income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 47-1806.03(a)(11) tax on` `the taxable income` MEANS
    foldl `take the row if it applies` 0 `the (a)(11) table`
    WHERE
        `take the row if it applies` `so far` `row` MEANS
            IF   `row`'s `over` EQUALS 0 OR `the taxable income` GREATER THAN `row`'s `over`
            THEN `row`'s `base amount` PLUS (`row`'s `rate` TIMES (max 0 (`the taxable income` MINUS `row`'s `over`)))
            ELSE `so far`

§§ `s 47-1806.01 -- taxable income`

-- "the entire net income of every resident, in excess of the personal exemptions and credits for dependents allowed by
-- § 47-1806.02". Net income is DC AGI less the standard or itemized deduction (s 47-1803.03; the standard deduction is the IRC
-- s 63(c) amount, s 47-1801.04(44)(iv)): an input.
DECLARE `DC return` HAS
    `taxable year`                              IS A NUMBER
    `resident for the whole taxable year`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `DC adjusted gross income`                  IS A NUMBER
    `standard or itemized deduction`            IS A NUMBER
    `number of personal exemptions`             IS A NUMBER
    `federal personal exemption amount`         IS A NUMBER
    `another taxpayer may claim the taxpayer as a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `federal earned income credit allowed`      IS A NUMBER
    `has a qualifying child for the earned income credit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earned income`                             IS A NUMBER
    `IRC s 32 credit percentage for no qualifying child` IS A NUMBER
    `IRC s 32 earned income amount for no qualifying child` IS A NUMBER
    `childless phaseout amount, as adjusted for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `qualifying children under 6 claimed as dependents` IS A NUMBER
    `filing as`                                 IS A `Child tax credit filing group`
    `resident for the whole preceding calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Child tax credit filing group` IS ONE OF
    `single, head of household, or qualifying widow(er)`
    `married or registered domestic partners, filing jointly or separately on a combined return`
    `married filing separately`

GIVEN `r` IS A `DC return`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the DC taxable income of` `r` MEANS
    max 0 (   `r`'s `DC adjusted gross income`
           MINUS `r`'s `standard or itemized deduction`
           MINUS `the DC personal exemptions for` (`r`'s `number of personal exemptions`) `of` (`r`'s `federal personal exemption amount`)
                     `at adjusted gross income` (`r`'s `DC adjusted gross income`)
                     `when another's dependent` (`r`'s `another taxpayer may claim the taxpayer as a dependent`))

§§ `s 47-1806.04(f) -- the DC earned income tax credit`

-- (f)(1)(B-1): from 2022, "an individual with a qualifying child who is allowed an earned income tax credit under section 32
-- ... shall be allowed a credit ... equal to 70% of the earned income tax credit allowed"; (B-2): from 2025, 85%; (B-3): from
-- 2029, 100%.
-- (C)(i): "an individual without a qualifying child who is eligible for an earned income tax credit on their federal tax return
-- under section 32 ... (without regard to the limit in section 32(a)(2) ...) shall be allowed a credit ... equal to the credit
-- percentage of so much of a taxpayer's earned income as does not exceed the earned income amount. (ii) The amount ... shall
-- not exceed the credit percentage of the earned income amount, over the phaseout percentage of 8.48% of so much of the
-- adjusted gross income (or, if greater, the earned income) ... as exceeds the phaseout amount of $17,235, increased annually by
-- the cost-of-living adjustment." The (A) 40% for any individual allowed the federal credit is read as displaced by (B-1) to
-- (B-3) and (C) for the people they describe (NOTES.md finding 4).
-- (f)(3)(A): "The credit ... shall be refundable".
GIVEN `the taxable year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the DC EITC percentage with a qualifying child for` `the taxable year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the taxable year` AT LEAST 2029 THEN 100%   -- (B-3)
        IF `the taxable year` AT LEAST 2025 THEN 85%    -- (B-2)
        OTHERWISE                                70%    -- (B-1)

GIVEN `r` IS A `DC return`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 47-1806.04(f) credit for` `r` MEANS
    IF   `r`'s `has a qualifying child for the earned income credit`
    THEN `the DC EITC percentage with a qualifying child for` (`r`'s `taxable year`) TIMES `r`'s `federal earned income credit allowed`
    ELSE max 0 (`the (C)(i) amount` MINUS `the (C)(ii) phaseout`)
    WHERE
        `p` MEANS `r`'s `IRC s 32 credit percentage for no qualifying child`
        `the (C)(i) amount` MEANS
            `p` TIMES min (`r`'s `earned income`) (`r`'s `IRC s 32 earned income amount for no qualifying child`)
        `the (C)(ii) phaseout` MEANS
            8.48% TIMES max 0 ((max (`r`'s `DC adjusted gross income`) (`r`'s `earned income`)) MINUS `r`'s `childless phaseout amount, as adjusted for the year`)

-- (f)(3)(B)(ii-a): "For taxable years beginning after December 31, 2023: (I) If the amount of the earned income tax credit
-- allowed is at least $1,200, the individual may elect ... whether the entire amount ... shall be paid ... in either 12 equal
-- monthly payments or one lump sum payment; or (II) If ... less than $1,200, the entire amount ... shall be paid ... in one lump
-- sum payment." (C): payments "shall not be considered income for the purpose of determining eligibility or benefit amount for
-- public assistance".
DECLARE `How the DC EITC is paid` IS ONE OF
    `I may elect 12 equal monthly payments or one lump sum`
    `one lump sum`

GIVEN `the credit allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `How the DC EITC is paid`
`how the DC EITC is paid, for a credit of` `the credit allowed` MEANS
    IF   `the credit allowed` AT LEAST 1200
    THEN `I may elect 12 equal monthly payments or one lump sum`
    ELSE `one lump sum`

§§ `s 47-1806.17 -- the child tax credit`

-- (a), (b)(1)(A): "For the taxable year beginning January 1, 2025, $420 for each qualifying child who has not reached the age
-- of 6 years by December 31, 2025, up to a maximum of 3 qualifying children". (b)(2): "reduced by $20 for each $1,000 (or
-- fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income exceeds the threshold amount; except, that the reductions
-- cannot reduce the credit below zero." (e)(5)(A): "$160,000 ... single, head of household, or qualifying widow(er); $240,000 in
-- the case of married individuals or registered domestic partners filing either jointly or separately on a combined return; or
-- $120,000 in the case of an individual filing as married filing separately." (c): refundable. (d): no credit if the child is
-- not claimed as a dependent on the federal and District returns, or "(2) The taxpayer was not a resident of the District for
-- the entire calendar year preceding the year in which a claim for this credit is filed."
GIVEN `the group` IS A `Child tax credit filing group`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2025 child tax credit threshold for` `the group` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the group`
    WHEN `single, head of household, or qualifying widow(er)` THEN 160000
    WHEN `married or registered domestic partners, filing jointly or separately on a combined return` THEN 240000
    WHEN `married filing separately` THEN 120000

GIVEN `r` IS A `DC return`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the s 47-1806.17 credit for` `r` MEANS
    IF   `r`'s `taxable year` LESS THAN 2025 OR `r`'s `qualifying children under 6 claimed as dependents` AT MOST 0
    THEN `answered` 0
    ELSE IF   `r`'s `taxable year` GREATER THAN 2025
         THEN `not covered` `the child tax credit after 2025 is increased by a cost-of-living adjustment that is not deposited (s 47-1806.17(b)(1)(B))`
         ELSE IF   NOT (`r`'s `resident for the whole preceding calendar year`)
              THEN `answered` 0
              ELSE `answered` (max 0 (`the full credit` MINUS `the reduction`))
    WHERE
        `the full credit` MEANS 420 TIMES min 3 (`r`'s `qualifying children under 6 claimed as dependents`)
        `the threshold` MEANS `the 2025 child tax credit threshold for` (`r`'s `filing as`)
        `the reduction` MEANS
            IF   `r`'s `DC adjusted gross income` GREATER THAN `the threshold`
            THEN 20 TIMES CEILING ((`r`'s `DC adjusted gross income` MINUS `the threshold`) DIVIDED BY 1000)
            ELSE 0

§§ `The balance`

-- The (a)(11) tax, less the earned income tax credit and the child tax credit, both refundable. Other credits, withholding and
-- estimated payments are not encoded.
GIVEN `r` IS A `DC return`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the DC income tax balance for` `r` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`r`'s `resident for the whole taxable year`)
    THEN `not covered` `the tax on a nonresident or part-year resident is not encoded`
    ELSE IF   `r`'s `taxable year` LESS THAN 2022
         THEN `not covered` `only taxable years beginning after December 31, 2021 are encoded (s 47-1806.03(a)(11))`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the s 47-1806.17 credit for` `r`
              WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
              WHEN `answered` `the child tax credit` THEN
                  `answered` (    `the s 47-1806.03(a)(11) tax on` (`the DC taxable income of` `r`)
                             MINUS `the s 47-1806.04(f) credit for` `r`
                             MINUS `the child tax credit`)

§§ `s 47-1805.02 -- who must file`

-- s 47-1805.02: "Each of the following persons shall file a return ...: (1) Every nonresident of the District receiving income
-- subject to tax pursuant to this chapter and every resident of the District, except a fiduciary, who is required to file a
-- federal return under the provisions of § 6012 of the Internal Revenue Code".
GIVEN `a resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `required to file a federal return under IRC s 6012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a resident who must file a DC return` IF
    `a resident` AND `required to file a federal return under IRC s 6012`

§§ `Filing, paying, deficiencies and appeals`

DECLARE `DC tax party` IS ONE OF
    `the taxpayer`
    `the person aggrieved by the assessment`

DECLARE `DC tax action` IS ONE OF
    `file the return and pay the tax due`
    `pay the deficiency`
    `appeal to the Superior Court`

-- s 47-1805.03(a)(2): "For tax years beginning after December 31, 2015, all returns of income for the preceding taxable year ...
-- shall be filed with the Chief Financial Officer on or before the 15th day of April of each year". s 47-1812.07(a)(1), (2):
-- the tax shown, beyond what was withheld or paid as estimated tax, "is due and payable in full at the time prescribed ... for
-- the filing of such return". Days from 1 January of the next year.
GIVEN `the taxable year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the DC due date for the calendar taxable year` `the taxable year` MEANS Date 15 4 (`the taxable year` PLUS 1)

-- s 47-1805.03(b): "The Chief Financial Officer may grant a reasonable extension of time for filing ... whenever in his judgment
-- good cause exists therefor ... Except in case of a taxpayer who is not within the continental limits of the United States, no
-- such extension shall be granted for more than 6 months, and in no case ... for more than 1 year." The extension granted is an
-- input, in days (0 if none); it moves the filing date only (s 47-1812.07(a) ties payment to "the time prescribed").
GIVEN `the taxable year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `DC tax party` `DC tax action`
`the duty to file the DC return and pay` `the taxable year` MEANS
    PARTY  `the taxpayer`
    MUST   `file the return and pay the tax due`
    WITHIN (Day (`the DC due date for the calendar taxable year` `the taxable year`) MINUS Day (Date 1 1 (`the taxable year` PLUS 1)))
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "return not filed or tax not paid by 15 April (ss 47-1805.03(a)(2), 47-1812.07(a)); the additions to tax are not in the deposited text"

GIVEN `outside the continental United States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest extension, in months, the Chief Financial Officer may grant` `outside the continental United States` MEANS
    IF `outside the continental United States` THEN 12 ELSE 6

-- s 47-1812.07(a)(3): "Any deficiency in any tax imposed by this chapter, determined by the Mayor under the provisions of
-- § 47-1812.05 shall be due and payable within 10 days from the date of the assessment."
-- s 47-1815.01: "Any person aggrieved by any assessment of a deficiency ... may, within 6 months from the date of the assessment
-- of the deficiency, appeal to the Superior Court of the District of Columbia". The six months are given in days by the
-- caller. An appeal not made is no breach (DO ... LEST FULFILLED; in the stable l4 a MAY would take its HENCE when the time
-- runs out unused).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `DC tax party` `DC tax action`
`the duty to pay an assessed deficiency` MEANS
    PARTY  `the taxpayer`
    MUST   `pay the deficiency`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "deficiency not paid within 10 days from the date of the assessment (s 47-1812.07(a)(3))"

GIVEN `days in the six months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `DC tax party` `DC tax action`
`the right to appeal a deficiency` `days in the six months` MEANS
    PARTY  `the person aggrieved by the assessment`
    DO     `appeal to the Superior Court`
    WITHIN `days in the six months`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   FULFILLED

§ `Questions for the taxpayer`

§§ `Am I a resident? Must I file?`

@export Am I a "resident" of the District of Columbia for income tax (s 47-1801.04(42))?
GIVEN `I was domiciled in DC at some time this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the District was your domicile (permanent legal home) at any time during the taxable year
      `days I kept a place of abode in DC` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in the taxable year you maintained a place to live in the District
      `I am an excluded federal official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an elected federal officer, a congressional staff member who is a bona fide resident of your member's state, a Senate-confirmed presidential appointee serving at the President's pleasure, or a Supreme Court Justice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a DC resident for income tax` IF
    `a resident of the District` `I was domiciled in DC at some time this year` `days I kept a place of abode in DC` `I am an excluded federal official`

@export Must I file a DC income tax return as a resident (s 47-1805.02(1))?
GIVEN `I am a DC resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a resident of the District for the year
      `I must file a federal return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are required to file a federal income tax return under IRC s 6012
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I file a DC return` IF `a resident who must file a DC return` `I am a DC resident` `I must file a federal return`

§§ `How much?`

@export What is the DC income tax on a given DC taxable income (s 47-1806.03(a)(11), years from 2022)?
GIVEN `my DC taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your DC taxable income in US dollars (DC adjusted gross income less the deduction and personal exemptions)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the DC tax on my taxable income` MEANS `the s 47-1806.03(a)(11) tax on` `my DC taxable income`

@export How much DC earned income tax credit do I get if I have a qualifying child (s 47-1806.04(f)(1)(B-1) to (B-3))?
GIVEN `the taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year of the return, 2022 or later
      `my federal earned income credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal earned income credit allowed to you under IRC s 32, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much DC EITC with a qualifying child` MEANS
    `the DC EITC percentage with a qualifying child for` `the taxable year` TIMES `my federal earned income credit`

@export How much DC earned income tax credit do I get with no qualifying child (s 47-1806.04(f)(1)(C))?
GIVEN `my earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your earned income for the year, in US dollars
      `my DC adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your DC adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `the federal credit percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The IRC s 32 credit percentage for a taxpayer with no qualifying child (for example 7.65%)
      `the federal earned income amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The IRC s 32 earned income amount for a taxpayer with no qualifying child for the year, in US dollars
      `the DC phaseout amount for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The DC phaseout amount: $17,235 increased by the cost-of-living adjustment for the year, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much DC EITC with no qualifying child` MEANS
    `the s 47-1806.04(f) credit for`
        (`DC return` OF 2025, TRUE, `my DC adjusted gross income`, 0, 0, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, `my earned income`,
                        `the federal credit percentage`, `the federal earned income amount`, `the DC phaseout amount for the year`,
                        0, `single, head of household, or qualifying widow(er)`, TRUE)
    -- only the earned income, AGI and the three s 32 figures are read by (f)(1)(C): the rest are fixed placeholders

@export Will my DC earned income tax credit be paid monthly or as a lump sum (s 47-1806.04(f)(3)(B)(ii-a))?
GIVEN `my DC earned income tax credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The DC earned income tax credit allowed to you, in US dollars
GIVETH A `How the DC EITC is paid`
`How will my DC EITC be paid` MEANS `how the DC EITC is paid, for a credit of` `my DC earned income tax credit`

@export How much DC child tax credit do I get for 2025 (s 47-1806.17)?
GIVEN `the taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year of the return (2025; later years need the cost-of-living adjusted amounts, not encoded)
      `my filing group` IS A `Child tax credit filing group` @desc How you file: single, head of household or qualifying widow(er); married or domestic partners filing jointly or separately on a combined return; or married filing separately
      `my DC adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your adjusted gross income on the return, in US dollars
      `qualifying children under 6` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying children (IRC s 24(c)) under age 6 at 31 December you claim as dependents on your federal and DC returns
      `I lived in DC all of last year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a resident of the District for the entire calendar year before the year you file the claim
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much DC child tax credit do I get` MEANS
    `the s 47-1806.17 credit for`
        (`DC return` OF `the taxable year`, TRUE, `my DC adjusted gross income`, 0, 0, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, 0, 0, 0,
                        `qualifying children under 6`, `my filing group`, `I lived in DC all of last year`)
    -- only the year, AGI, children, filing group and the preceding year's residence are read: the rest are fixed placeholders

@export How much DC income tax do I owe after the earned income and child tax credits (negative means a refund)?
GIVEN `the taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year of the return, 2022 or later
      `I was a DC resident all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a resident of the District for the whole taxable year
      `my DC adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your DC adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `my deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc Your standard deduction (the federal IRC s 63(c) amount) or your itemized deductions, in US dollars
      `my personal exemptions` IS A NUMBER @desc How many personal exemptions you have under s 47-1806.02 (yourself, a spouse with no income, dependents, and so on)
      `the federal exemption amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The personal exemption amount prescribed in IRC s 151 for the year, in US dollars (nil for years in which the federal amount is nil)
      `someone can claim me as a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another taxpayer can claim you as a dependent
      `my federal earned income credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal earned income credit allowed to you, in US dollars (0 if none)
      `I have a qualifying child for the EITC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a qualifying child for the earned income credit
      `my filing group` IS A `Child tax credit filing group` @desc How you file, for the child tax credit threshold
      `qualifying children under 6` IS A NUMBER @desc Qualifying children under 6 you claim as dependents
      `I lived in DC all of last year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a District resident for the entire preceding calendar year
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much DC income tax do I owe` MEANS
    `the DC income tax balance for`
        (`DC return` OF `the taxable year`, `I was a DC resident all year`, `my DC adjusted gross income`, `my deduction`,
                        `my personal exemptions`, `the federal exemption amount`, `someone can claim me as a dependent`,
                        `my federal earned income credit`, `I have a qualifying child for the EITC`, 0, 0, 0, 0,
                        `qualifying children under 6`, `my filing group`, `I lived in DC all of last year`)
    -- the childless EITC computation is its own question: here a filer with no qualifying child gets it only through that
    -- question (its figures are placeholders of nil, which give nil)

§§ `When?`

@export By what date must I file my DC return and pay the tax, for a calendar taxable year (s 47-1805.03(a)(2))?
GIVEN `the taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year of the return, for example 2025
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I file and pay in DC` MEANS `the DC due date for the calendar taxable year` `the taxable year`

@export For how many months at most may the Chief Financial Officer extend my time to file (s 47-1805.03(b))?
GIVEN `I am outside the continental United States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are outside the continental limits of the United States
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How long an extension may I get` MEANS `the longest extension, in months, the Chief Financial Officer may grant` `I am outside the continental United States`

@export I have been assessed a DC income tax deficiency: by what date must I pay it (s 47-1812.07(a)(3))?
GIVEN `the date of the assessment` IS A DATE @desc The date of the assessment of the deficiency
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I pay the deficiency` MEANS `the date of the assessment` PLUS 10
